    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87YVifT",
      "title": "ci: standardize image builds on factory plan action",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 616,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nConsolidates `branches.yaml` and `tags.yaml` into a single `build-images.yaml` that calls `ethereum-optimism/factory/actions/plan`. The plan action unifies the legacy `detect-changes` (branch / PR pushes) and `parse-tag` (release tag pushes) flows behind a single matrix output, so one job covers every trigger type.\n\nThis iteration also collapses the legacy `local` + `fork` build pair into a single `build` job. The factory reusable now exposes a composite `actions/fork-context` action that resolves the effective registry (`canonical` on non-fork, `ttl.sh/<sha>` on fork) and gates GCP auth + provenance attestation internally, so callers no longer need to fork policy at the matrix level. See [factory#37](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/factory/pull/37).\n\n- Pins the factory references (plan action and reusable workflow) to `aced2657632c849ce64a84cc72e3d2940883d374` from `factory#37`.\n- Drops `matrix.x || 'default'` passthroughs for inputs that the factory reusable already defaults (`mode`, `target`, `build_args`, `skip_arm64`); only the inputs that `images.json` actually populates (`context`, `dockerfile`, `image_name`) are forwarded explicitly.\n- `build` job carries `id-token: write` and `attestations: write` permissions; the reusable will only exercise them on non-fork events thanks to the new `should_authenticate` output of the composite action.\n- `images.json` unchanged except for the prior `shared_paths` update.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] CI passes on this PR (non-fork path validates; fork path is symmetric and isolated in the composite action).\n- [x] `plan` emits an empty matrix on this PR since only workflow/config files changed and `build` is skipped.\n- [ ] After merge, a follow-up PR touching an image source directory builds only the affected images.\n- [ ] A release tag (e.g. `proxyd/vX.Y.Z`) builds and tags exactly that image at the parsed version.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-05T09:29:21Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-05-05T12:50:21Z",
      "additions": 50,
      "deletions": 92
    },
